// How the ore storage is shown (WP7.3, docs/rules/economy.md, "Storage"). Read by
// sf_data::storage_look, compiled into the game, and checked when it is parsed. Presentation only:
// what a structure stores is `storage` in the building block of unit_defs.ron, and no checksum
// depends on this file.
//
// Every standing structure that stores ore (the refinery) carries a bar under its front edge, the
// same place and the same sizes as the progress bar of a structure under construction (which it
// replaces once the structure is complete). The bar is the owner's whole store: stored ore out of
// the capacity of all the owner's standing storing structures, so every refinery of a player
// shows the same fill. Colours sRGB, alpha last. Sizes in logical pixels: no bar when the edge is
// narrower than `min_width_px` on the screen, never wider than `max_width_px`, `gap_px` below the
// edge.
(
    bar: (
        fill: (240, 170, 40, 235),
        back: (10, 14, 20, 190),
        height_px: 6,
        min_width_px: 18,
        max_width_px: 220,
        gap_px: 4,
    ),
    // The fill of a full store: the harvesters wait.
    full: (255, 90, 60, 245),
)
